# --- CV data: personal by default, and deliberately not committable ---------
# cv/master.yaml is the fact base: a real name, email address, phone number,
# employment history and the full achievement bank. It is ignored at the
# DIRECTORY level rather than by file, so a new file added beside it (another
# summary variant, an exported CV, a notes file) cannot slip into a commit by
# being unlisted. Ed's instruction, 2026-09-23: "ignore all the cv folders in
# git. I don't plan on pushing it just yet but we can check when I come to do
# that."
#
# The vendored engine's CODE and DOCUMENTATION are deliberately NOT ignored —
# scripts/ and templates/ are machine, not facts, and belong in the repo. The
# split is facts-vs-machine, and it is drawn here rather than in per-directory
# .gitignore files so anyone auditing what could ever be pushed sees it in one
# place.
#
# context/ is the exception, added 2026-09-23 when the fork went public:
# context/01-data-model.md carries the same fact base as cv/master.yaml — a
# real name, email address, phone number and location — so reading it as
# "machine documentation" was wrong. It is ignored at the DIRECTORY level for
# the same reason cv/ is: a new note dropped beside these docs must not reach a
# public commit by being unlisted.
cv/
cv_output/
context/
#
# contract.yaml joins them for the same reason, from the other direction: it is
# live config the pipeline reads, but the one personal number in it is the
# target salary. contract.yaml.example is committed in its place, and is what
# app/contract_rates.py falls back to, so a fresh clone still runs.
contract.yaml

# --- QA / E2E -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Playwright's build output for the test server (see web/next.config.js's
# NEXT_DIST_DIR) and the generated fixture board. Neither is source.
web/.next-e2e/
web/e2e/.fixtures/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/
